  "body": "## What changed\n\nTwo pinning tests, no code change. They pin the two review notes of commit `d41c2b76a` on PR #3577 in their current form on `main`.\n\nMain has moved since the notes were written: #3748 retired the automatic dead-end ramp, and #3884 reworked the stand-in notes. The old note text \"instead of the helix entry\" and `StartSide::ramp_fallback_note` no longer exist. The pins assert the same laws on the current wording.\n\n## The pins\n\n- `machining2d::pass_start::tests::the_fallback_note_counts_once_as_the_pass_start_cause` (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/pass_start.rs`): the start-side fallback note counts one time in `pass_start_fallbacks`, so the operation names the cause `FallbackCause::PassStart`, never \"Adaptive fell back\"; two notes count two.\n- `the_replaced_helix_entry_is_named_once_on_the_band_path` (`crates/motion/tests/pass_start_engagement.rs`): on the band path with the selected Helix entry, the advice note names the entry exactly one time, and no \" - helix entry instead\" stand-in note is written beside it.\n\n## Readings\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-motion --lib`: 737 passed, 0 failed, 22 ignored.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-motion --test pass_start_engagement`: 9 passed, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo app-level warning path and no posted program: the diff touches motion tests only.\n\n## Origin branch note\n\n`origin/issue/3734-dead-end-ramp-pins` (commit `9d260b2f5`, author `NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>`) holds the two pins in their pre-#3748 form. It is not this fork's branch, so it was not reused or rebased.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nRefs #3734\r\n",
